Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:06:36 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] Fix remaining bugs: tty prompts, SSL renewal/port 80, token,
 Docker restart, GPG fingerprint

- All scripts: read prompts from /dev/tty via ask() helper (fd 3), so
  `curl ... | sudo bash` works; clear error and exit 1 when no TTY.
- All scripts: OS version check (Ubuntu 20.04+, Debian 11+); empty or
  non-numeric VERSION_ID (Debian testing/sid) is allowed with a warning.
- install-ssl.sh:
  - only standalone mode checks/frees port 80; webroot and nginx keep
    the web server running
  - stopped service/container is restarted on success AND failure
    (EXIT trap); standalone saves certbot pre/post hooks so renewals
    stop/start the same service
  - manual DNS: explicit "no auto-renew" warnings, renewal dry-run
    skipped; new option 5: DNS via Cloudflare plugin (token hidden,
    stored mode 600) for auto-renewing wildcard certs
  - certbot command built as an array (no eval, no *.domain globbing),
    with --cert-name so the dry-run targets this certificate only
  - dpkg-query status check instead of `dpkg -l | grep`
- clone-repo.sh: token removed from .git/config after clone (remote
  reset to clean URL); optional per-repo credential file (mode 600);
  token variable unset; deploy key / fine-grained token advice.
- install-docker.sh:
  - Docker GPG key accepted only if fingerprint matches
    9DC858229FC7DD38854AE2D88D81803C0EBFCD88 (also for mirror keys);
    otherwise docker-ce repos are skipped (distro fallback only)
  - daemon.json written only if content changed; Docker restarted only
    if changed, with confirmation when containers are running
  - "Idempotent" claim replaced by accurate re-run behaviour
- tunnel-install.sh: no pinned checksum (i386/armhf) requires explicit
  confirmation (default abort); network-manager-openvpn now optional
  (default no); guarded cd.
- README: recommend `sudo bash -c "$(curl -fsSL URL)"`, download-then-run
  and pinning to a commit SHA; document all of the above.
